"""Generate an English report from executed Experiment 2 artifacts."""
import json
import statistics
from pathlib import Path


def mean(values):
    values=[float(x) for x in values if x!='N/A' and x is not None]
    return statistics.mean(values) if values else 'N/A'


def f(x):
    return f'{x:.6f}' if isinstance(x,float) else str(x)


def table(fields,rows):
    safe=lambda x:f(x).replace('|','\\|').replace('\n',' ')
    return ['| '+' | '.join(fields)+' |','| '+' | '.join(['---']*len(fields))+' |']+['| '+' | '.join(safe(x) for x in row)+' |' for row in rows]


def build_report(out,coverage,pools,baseline,summary,relevance,runtime):
    available=sum(r['original_sidecar_description_present'] for r in coverage)
    usable=sum(r['usable_description'] for r in coverage)
    new=sum(r['overlay_description_added'] for r in coverage)
    full=[r for r in baseline if r['pool_id']=='catalogue3568']
    full75=[r for r in summary if r['pool_id']=='catalogue3568' and r['requested_percent']==75]
    review=json.loads((out/'source_review.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
    semantic=(out/'semantic_metadata.json').exists()
    methods=['A','B','C']+(['D'] if semantic else [])
    doc=['# Experiment 2: POI enrichment coverage and ranking robustness','',
         '## Findings and decision','',
         f'The canonical catalogue contains 3,570 POIs and no narrative-description column. The supplied 40-POI enrichment file contains {available} descriptions. One missing summary was resolved through a precise municipal name/address match in a separate overlay. After retaining the two disputed records as exclusions, {usable} source-supported descriptions are usable for this experiment: {usable/3570:.2%} of the canonical catalogue ({usable}/3,570), or {usable/3568:.2%} of the 3,568 eligible rows. This is the practical coverage constraint; the selected enriched subset is not representative of catalogue-wide narrative coverage.','',
         'Both lexical methods can assign finite scores across the eligible catalogue using taxonomy metadata, including rows without descriptions. Finite score coverage is computational coverage, not a guarantee of a meaningful query match. Coverage, query overlap, ties and ranking stability are therefore reported separately. No broader-pool relevance labels were created.','',
         'Recommendation: retain a cached taxonomy-only lexical control as the default for subsequent isolated large-catalogue work, and test description-aware scoring only with explicit source/coverage tracking and a same-model metadata projection when descriptions are absent. B is unchanged by description masking by construction; that stability does not establish superior relevance. Do not blend raw B/C/A similarity or preference scores per POI. This experiment supports preparing a controlled GFAR comparison, not adopting a production scorer. GFAR integration itself was not performed.','',
         '## Scope and frozen design','',
         'The original Round 1 artifacts and completed Phase 1 exploratory evaluation were read only. The 12 frozen Korean scenario texts and their original ten-feature preference vectors were reused. New candidate pools contain multiple original feature signatures, so the binary baseline is no longer forced to tie every candidate. All methods see the identical candidate identities within each pool. No canonical data, binary feature values, production scorer, GFAR, schemas, application files or original human ratings were changed.','',
         'Two domains avoid silently redefining the original methods. In original_fields, B uses detailed_category, food_type, representative_menu and activity_type; C adds description_summary. This is a new 38-POI experiment using the original allowlist, not a replacement for the 19-POI frozen model. In taxonomy_extension, B uses category_name plus source-supported food/menu/activity fields where present; C adds usable summaries. The latter are explicitly broader variants of B/C because canonical rows lack detailed_category and other enrichment fields. D uses the same expanded text as C in the applicable domain; A calls the actual production score_individuals function. Place names, addresses, collection metadata, previous scores, selection labels and human grades are excluded from ranking text.','',
         'B and C are fitted separately once per domain on all eligible documents before scoring, using the original within-token character 2/3-gram TF-IDF rules, smoothed IDF and L2 normalization. Queries are excluded from fitting. Vocabulary/IDF are then held fixed for all candidate pools and masks within that domain. Different pool sizes do not change the corpus or fit. The full-catalogue corpus may be used because this is an unsupervised indexing diagnostic, not a held-out relevance generalization test. No hyperparameter or scoring-rule tuning was performed.','',
         ('D was executed offline with the existing pinned multilingual MiniLM model, CPU float32, normalized embeddings, deterministic eval and one torch thread. Unique text deduplication avoids repeating identical taxonomy embeddings; repeat embeddings were byte identical. Empty text is explicitly uninformative (zero vector), never a meaningful empty-string embedding.' if semantic else 'D was not requested; no semantic results are inferred.'),'',
         'Pool memberships and model inputs were frozen before any comparison scores. Smaller mixed pools anchor all 38 eligible enriched records, guarantee every eligible feature signature, and add seeded canonical distractors. This deliberately tests dilution under increasing candidate counts; its inflated narrative prevalence must not be interpreted as representative random coverage. Three seeded nested samples at 100, 500 and 1,000 candidates retain sampling sensitivity. The complete 3,568-row eligible catalogue supplies the least selection-dependent coverage diagnostic.','']
    headline=[]
    for m in methods:
        headline.append(f'{m}={mean([r["exact_tied_pair_fraction"] for r in full if r["method"]==m]):.2%}')
    doc[doc.index('## Scope and frozen design'):doc.index('## Scope and frozen design')]=[
        '### What changed when candidate pools broadened','',
        'Mean exact tied-pair fractions on the complete eligible catalogue are '+', '.join(headline)+'. Thus B/C do not consistently reduce global ties relative to the binary baseline in broader pools. Most lexical ties arise from zero query overlap; metadata-only B has all-zero full-catalogue scores for S07 and S12. D produces fewer ties but that separation is not relevance evidence.','',
        'At 75% additional masking, mean top-10 retention is '+', '.join(f'{r["policy"]}={r["mean_topk_id_retention"]:.2%}' for r in full75 if r['policy'] in ['C_native','D_native'])+'. Catalogue-wide stability can conceal sensitivity in enriched subgroups: most full-catalogue rows never had descriptions to lose.','',
        'On the original human-annotated groups, the mean of the two sheet-specific macro NDCGs at 0% → 75% masking is '+', '.join(f'{m}: {mean([r["mean_scenario_macro_ndcg"] for r in relevance if r["requested_percent"]==0 and r["method"]==m]):.6f} → {mean([r["mean_scenario_macro_ndcg"] for r in relevance if r["requested_percent"]==75 and r["method"]==m]):.6f}' for m in ['B','C']+(['D'] if semantic else []))+'. C’s small initial advantage over B is not robust at this masking level; the slightly reversed descriptive means are not evidence of a significant difference. D’s broader-list stability does not prevent a larger relevance-sensitivity loss on the selected annotated groups.',''
    ]
    doc+=table(['Pool','Domain','POIs','Feature signatures','Usable descriptions','Description fraction'],[[r['pool_id'],r['domain'],r['candidate_count'],r['feature_signatures'],r['usable_descriptions'],r['description_fraction']] for r in pools])
    doc+=['','## Coverage and source audit','',
          'Coverage is assessed across the canonical file joined by exact stable IDs to the frozen 40-POI enrichment file and one narrowly sourced overlay. A usable description requires nonempty normalized narrative, dated field-level source provenance, and no unresolved primary identity/feature exclusion. Existing evidence comes from the supplied audit; only the eight targeted issues received a new bounded web review. Source-supported does not mean every statement was independently reverified today. Detailed category strings are metadata, not narrative coverage. Missing/NULL information is never an absent attribute or a negative relevance label.','',
          'Coverage by canonical source:','']
    doc+=table(['Source','POIs','Original sidecar descriptions','Usable descriptions','Usable fraction'],[[source,len(rs),sum(r['original_sidecar_description_present'] for r in rs),sum(r['usable_description'] for r in rs),sum(r['usable_description'] for r in rs)/len(rs)] for source in sorted({r['source'] for r in coverage}) for rs in [[r for r in coverage if r['source']==source]]])
    from run_robustness import read_csv
    bycat=read_csv(out/'coverage_by_category.csv')
    doc+=['','Coverage by top-level taxonomy; detailed binary-feature and signature coverage is also retained in coverage_by_category.csv. Binary feature groups overlap and should not be summed.','']
    doc+=table(['Taxonomy group','POIs','In 40-POI file','Usable descriptions','Usable fraction'],[[r['group_value'],r['canonical_pois'],r['enriched_40_pois'],r['usable_descriptions'],float(r['usable_description_fraction'])] for r in bycat if r['group_dimension']=='taxonomy_top'])
    doc+=['','### Two conflicts and six missing descriptions','',
          'One of six missing summaries was resolved; five remain missing after the bounded search. The Tavolo restaurant attribute is confirmed, but its original café binary feature remains unchanged and disputed for fair model comparison. The birthplace/memorial address conflict remains unresolved. Both records remain excluded from all primary scoring pools; they remain visible in the 3,570-row audit. No speculative repairs were needed to proceed.','']
    doc+=table(['POI ID','Issue','Disposition','Source and evidence limit'],[[r['place_id'],r['issue'],r['status'],(f'[source]({r["source_url"]}) ' if r['source_url'] else '')+r['identity_evidence']] for r in review['records']])
    doc+=['',
          'The [Dong-gu facility listing](https://www.bsdonggu.go.kr/board/view.donggu?boardId=BBS_0000201&dataSid=5053866&menuCd=DOM_000000104008001002&paging=ok&startPage=4) matches 수정산가족체육공원 at 수정공원로63-1 and records exercise facilities. The overlay summarizes those facts without transferring nearby playground rules or claiming current access. The [university facilities table](https://www.pknu.ac.kr/main/118) identifies Tavolo as a restaurant; it does not supply a revised ten-feature vector. The [Seo-gu birthplace listing](https://www.bsseogu.go.kr/tour/board/view.do?boardId=BBS_0000084&dataSid=5030&menuCd=DOM_000000304006000000&startPage=1) still gives a different address; this review obtained its search excerpt while a full-page fetch timed out. No ambiguous merge was made.','',
          '## Baseline ranking diagnostics','',
          'Exact tied-pair fraction counts all unordered candidate pairs with exactly equal native scores, divided by n(n−1)/2. No rounding or tolerance-based tie breaking was used. K=min(10, pool size) for these unlabeled diagnostics. NDCG continues to use its original K=min(3, candidate-group size) only in the annotated sensitivity section. Raw score magnitudes are not compared across algorithms.','']
    for poolid in ['enriched38','catalogue3568']:
        doc+=[f'### {poolid}','']
        doc+=table(['Method','Mean exact-tie fraction','Mean distinct bands','Mean positive-score fraction (text methods)','Queries with all zero scores'],[[m,mean([r['exact_tied_pair_fraction'] for r in baseline if r['pool_id']==poolid and r['method']==m]),mean([r['distinct_score_bands'] for r in baseline if r['pool_id']==poolid and r['method']==m]),mean([r['positive_score_fraction'] for r in baseline if r['pool_id']==poolid and r['method']==m]) if m!='A' else 'N/A: survey scale always positive',sum(r['score_max']==0 for r in baseline if r['pool_id']==poolid and r['method']==m)] for m in methods])
    doc+=['','All individual query/pool/method rows, native score ranges and dispersion are preserved in baseline_ranking_diagnostics.csv. baseline_top10.csv retains ID-fallback rankings, scores, source-description availability and feature signatures. between_method_ranking_changes.csv reports top-K and rank-correlation differences across each pair of methods without converting those differences into accuracy.','',
          '## Missing-description perturbation and fallbacks','',
          f'Five requested mask levels (0%, 10%, 25%, 50%, 75%) apply to the {usable} available, usable descriptions, not to all 3,568 rows. Naturally missing descriptions remain missing. Five seed permutations (11, 29, 47, 71, 101) give nested masked-ID sets within each seed; integer counts use floor(n×p+0.5). The zero-mask case is executed once, giving 21 configurations. Exact selected IDs, requested and realized fractions are saved. The same global mask is applied to all methods and pools, so a small annotated subgroup can have a realized rate different from the global rate. No IDF refit follows masking. This isolates missing fields rather than conflating missingness with retraining.','',
          'Policies: C_native removes the description and re-encodes remaining metadata in the same fixed C vector space. D_native does the equivalent with the same pinned encoder. B_global ignores descriptions for every candidate. B_backbone_C_ties orders lexicographically by B then C within exact B ties, and never adds or compares raw values from two scales; its exported intermediate band codes are ordinal, so positivity/ranges are N/A. C_described_only abstains when a description is unavailable; abstention is tracked as unrankable while retaining the original candidate identity list and coverage denominator. It is a coverage diagnostic, not a fair all-candidate relevance comparison.','',
          'Each policy is compared against its own unmasked baseline. ID retention is the fraction of baseline top-K items retained; Jaccard uses the union denominator. A separate tie-aware measure compares top-K membership-probability distributions: sum(min(p_before,p_after))/min(K, baseline rankable count), with uniform membership within exact tied bands. This is distribution overlap, not the expected overlap of two independent sampled rankings. Identical fully tied outputs can score stability 1 without being informative. Spearman uses average ranks for exact ties; it is N/A if either common rank vector is constant, and its jointly rankable denominator is retained.','',
          'Full-catalogue masking results (C_native and D_native):','']
    doc+=table(['Mask %','Policy','Rankable fraction','Positive-score fraction','ID top-10 retention','Tie-aware probability overlap','Mean Spearman','Undefined correlations'],[[r['requested_percent'],r['policy'],r['mean_rankable_fraction'],r['mean_positive_score_fraction'],r['mean_topk_id_retention'],r['mean_topk_membership_probability_overlap'],r['mean_spearman_average_tie_ranks'],r['undefined_spearman_rows']] for r in summary if r['pool_id']=='catalogue3568' and r['policy'] in ['C_native','D_native']])
    doc+=['','At 75% additional description masking, fallback comparison on the full catalogue:','']
    doc+=table(['Policy','Rankable fraction','ID top-10 retention','Worst query/seed ID retention','Mean returned top-10 length','Tie fraction'],[[r['policy'],r['mean_rankable_fraction'],r['mean_topk_id_retention'],r['min_topk_id_retention'],r['mean_topk_returned'],r['mean_exact_tied_pair_fraction']] for r in full75])
    doc+=['','The same summaries exist for all 11 pools; masking_robustness.csv retains all scenario/seed rows. Complete-case abstention reports tied pairs among rankable items only, so a low tie rate in that policy must be read alongside its low catalogue coverage. B_global stability is a mathematical consequence of ignoring the masked fields. Neither that result nor a small Spearman change proves relevance under missing information.','',
          '## Relevance sensitivity on existing annotations only','',
          'This section restores the original Round 1 B/C vocabulary and IDF, original A/B/C/D scores, original candidate groups and original query embeddings. At zero masking, every per-sheet NDCG result exactly matches the completed Phase 1 output. For masked C/D candidates, only the description contribution is removed; metadata projections are computed with the original fixed model. Expanded pools receive no NDCG or manufactured relevance labels. The original original_fields/taxonomy_extension newly fitted models are not evaluated against partial labels from a larger candidate set.','',
          'R1 and R2 are legacy sheet IDs completed by ONE model-blinded person. They are not independent raters. We keep the two label sets separate and report their equal-weight descriptive mean below without claiming consensus ground truth. The unresolved S01 grade rationale and S05 missing-information note remain documented in Phase 1; ratings were not corrected or tuned against this experiment.','']
    relrows=[]
    for rate in [0,10,25,50,75]:
        for m in methods:
            a=next(r for r in relevance if r['requested_percent']==rate and r['method']==m and r['sheet_id']=='R1')
            b=next(r for r in relevance if r['requested_percent']==rate and r['method']==m and r['sheet_id']=='R2')
            relrows.append([rate,m,a['mean_scenario_macro_ndcg'],b['mean_scenario_macro_ndcg'],mean([a['mean_scenario_macro_ndcg'],b['mean_scenario_macro_ndcg']]),a['min_seed_macro_ndcg'],a['max_seed_macro_ndcg'],b['min_seed_macro_ndcg'],b['max_seed_macro_ndcg']])
    doc+=table(['Mask %','Method','Sheet A mean NDCG','Sheet B mean NDCG','Mean of sheet means','A seed min','A seed max','B seed min','B seed max'],relrows)
    doc+=['','Seed ranges describe sensitivity to selected missing descriptions and are not confidence intervals. A/B are unchanged by construction in this analysis. Candidate sets with any insufficient judgment would be excluded as in the original evaluator; zero ideal DCG remains N/A. Exact exclusions, pairwise agreement, candidate counts and actual masked counts are retained in annotated_mask_metrics.csv. No significance or population-generalization claim is made.','',
          '## Runtime','',
          'Latency measurements separate one-time offline model load, B/C fitting, document/query encoding and warm query score-plus-sort. The table reports medians for cached query/document vectors: candidate vector gathering, dot-product or production score calculation, and deterministic full sorting are included. Text/query encoding, model load, corpus fitting, network, database access and UI are excluded from those medians. Twelve queries × three repeats per pool/method were measured on this machine. runtime_measurements.csv also records single-query lexical/transformer encoding, so warm-ranking timings are not presented as end-to-end service latency. No cross-machine speed claim is made.','']
    doc+=table(['Pool','Method','Candidates','Median warm score/sort ms','p95 ms'],[[r['pool_id'],r['method'],r['candidates'],r['warm_score_sort_median_ms'],r['warm_score_sort_p95_ms']] for r in runtime if r['pool_id'] in ['enriched38','mixed100_seed11','mixed500_seed11','mixed1000_seed11','catalogue3568']])
    doc+=['','## Interpretation and limits','',
          'The experiment establishes available-data coverage, finite-score coverage, sensitivity to specified random description loss, and deterministic ranking behaviour under broader candidate pools. It does not establish relevance improvement in the new pools: they have no judgments. Rank differentiation, positive lexical overlap and stability are diagnostics. The 12 synthetic requests remain narrowly drawn from the original enrichment evidence and do not represent real user demand or discovery of new preferences.','',
          'Naturally missing descriptions are highly nonrandom: the catalogue is dominated by records outside the curated 40-POI file. Additional random masking of the available descriptions is a conditional stress test and does not simulate the full real acquisition process. Anchored smaller pools deliberately retain all described cases; compare against the full-catalogue coverage before judging practicality. Five random seeds do not create independent user data.','',
          'The new municipal description is not part of any annotated candidate group, so it can alter broader rankings but cannot acquire a human relevance grade by transfer. Source summaries have varied retrieval modes and dates. Preserved identity/category exclusions protect against inaccurate joins, but the remaining inherited evidence is not a new field-by-field ground-truth validation. Semantic outputs may depend on hardware/library precision despite deterministic repeats here.','',
          'For a subsequent GFAR experiment, freeze groups, candidate pools, data coverage, fallback handling and score calibration separately. Compare the existing baseline and experimental individual scorer on identical pools, report per-member and minimum utility alongside group mean/disparity and returned-list coverage, and distinguish model-derived utility from independent satisfaction. The present cosine scores are not calibrated 1–5 utilities. Proceed with controlled offline integration work only; production adoption still requires adequate independent relevance and group-level evidence.','',
          '## Reproducibility and deliverables','',
          'config.json, freeze_manifest.json and pre_scoring_freeze.json record fixed rules, source/code hashes, environment, seeds, model identity, candidate membership and exact model text before scoring. lexical_models.json retains both domain-specific vocabularies/IDFs; scores_original_fields.npz and scores_taxonomy_extension.npz retain native full baseline and metadata-projection matrices in model_inputs.csv order, with scenario order in scenarios.json. description_masks.json identifies every removed narrative.','',
          'verification.json records original source hashes, protected code/data preservation, zero-mask Phase 1 reproduction and exact command. The original strict tracked-key verifier rejects two Phase 1 analysis scripts committed after the old freeze; the new experiment verifies every original protected key/hash, permits only those two known additions, and protects the full current tracked snapshot before/after. Its exact disposition is preserved. output_hashes.json hashes completed files. The test log and repeat-comparison record are supplied after validation. Runtime data and timestamp/environment manifests are kept separate from deterministic ranking artifacts. A new output directory is required on every run; earlier results are never overwritten. No private repository settings, credentials, database requests or external messages were used.','',
          'Main outputs: robustness_report.md; coverage_by_poi.csv and coverage_by_category.csv; enrichment_issue_audit.csv, description_overlay.csv and source_review.json; candidate_pools.csv and pool_memberships.csv; baseline_ranking_diagnostics.csv, baseline_top10.csv and between_method_ranking_changes.csv; masking_robustness.csv and masking_summary.csv; annotated_mask_metrics.csv and annotated_mask_summary.csv; runtime_measurements.csv and runtime_summary.csv; configuration, fitted-model and preservation files described above.','']
    (out/'robustness_report.md').write_text('\n'.join(doc)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
